{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
  "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Eric D. Miller",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In an individual capacity action against a government employee, the plaintiff seeks relief from the employee personally. The judgment is not enforceable against the government. For that reason, such an action does not implicate sovereign immunity. This Court has repeatedly applied that principle to individual capacity actions against federal and state employees, and it applies equally when the defendant is an employee of an Indian tribe."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They say it's the same as if it were federal employee, then you would have the Westfall Act. If it was a state employee, you would have the same regime, and the tribe says, \"And we do the same thing.\" You can sue in our court just as you could sue in federal court under the Westfall Act -- Connecticut court under the Connecticut Act, and you can sue in our court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why shouldn't we? I mean, you suggest the difference is because this is a voluntary agreement. But why shouldn't it be the rule that if the State pays, we should understand it to be a suit against the State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. What would we write that you think would affect official immunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. O'Conell (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We wouldn't want the Court to write anything in its opinion about tribal sovereign immunity that would preclude a defense of official immunity from being raised in this case or by other tribal employees sued in the future."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Do you think that might have happened here in the court below, in the Connecticut courts, that those two concepts were confused?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Now, on the facts of this case, is there any argument in favor of official immunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. O'Conell (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For official immunity, based on the facts as you've described them and as I understand them, no. Driving is -- is a quintessential activity that involves no policymaking authority. I think the Federal Drivers Act shows that and cases of this Court show that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Well, Mr. Clarke is arguing that if you're going to go back to the common law official immunity doctrine, that covered, as our Westfall case indicated, even nondiscretionary acts; that it covered every act. What's your position on that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As Justice Ginsburg noted, the Mohegan tribe is asking for the same protections from suit that every other sovereign enjoys. If Clarke were a Federal employee, a foreign employee, or a Connecticut State one, this suit would be barred. There's no reason the rule should be different for tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so if the tribe's waived sovereign immunity, why shouldn't the individual?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any -- is there any court that has held that an indemnification agreement, agreement to indemnify the employee, extends sovereign immunity to that employee?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Correct. If -- if there were no indemnification agreement or anything like that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why should -- why should a -- a tribal employee driving a limo be entitled to official immunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Miller",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the question of official immunity, we've already discussed the reasons why it's not part of the case before this Court, but I'd like to add that this case is a particularly bad vehicle with which to consider the -- in which to consider the question of official immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f869b1b1e4b97621db3f42af5c77c3dfbb12cac2e2c2538b07dcd51e1be86fdf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f869b1b1e4b9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think, Mr. Miller, that there's any decision that precludes us from saying that we're going to treat this as sovereign immunity or not sovereign immunity depending on an -- an indemnification agreement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1500",
      "confidence": 0.0,
